# uv's lockfile. NOT committed, deliberately. tools/rustconv/pyproject.toml is the
# authoritative pin (it hard-pins the tree-sitter parsers, and its own comment records
# why: an audit once ran under a stray tree-sitter 0.26.0 while the venv held 0.25.2, so
# the "clean" result had to be re-derived). Nothing in this repo invokes uv, and a second
# lockfile that nobody maintains is the same drift hazard wearing a different hat — a
# months-old `uv sync` would resolve the FLOORED deps to whatever was current when it was
# written and look perfectly clean doing it. Regenerate locally with `uv lock` if you want
# one; it is not shared state.
uv.lock
*.egg-info/
sdk/lib/rust/rust-kernel-target/
sdk/lib/rust/target/
ntoskrnl/rust-kernel-target/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
sdk/lib/rust/ntoskrnl-rust/src/pnpmgr/devaction_codex.rs.bak

# Build directories and toolchain
.build-tools
.build-tools/
build-amd64/
build-arm64/
build-i386/

# QEMU binary images (tracked scripts are fine)
qemu/*.img
qemu/*.qcow2
qemu/*.fd
# ...but DO track the canonical UEFI firmware blobs so every worktree boots
# without manual provisioning (OVMF32 = i386/amd64 UEFI; QEMU_EFI/efivars = arm64).
!qemu/OVMF32_CODE.fd
!qemu/OVMF32_VARS.fd
!qemu/QEMU_EFI.fd
!qemu/efivars.fd
qemu/*.efi
qemu/*.map
qemu/*.png
qemu/*.ppm
qemu/*.log
qemu/*.hdd.img
qemu/reactos_*.qcow2

# API keys
.env

# Claude Code runtime state (lock files, agent scratch, project memory)
.claude/

# OpenAI Codex runtime state (codex creates both .codex/ dir and .codex file)
.codex
.codex/

# Host tools cmake artifacts (from in-tree configure)
Makefile
cmake_install.cmake
qemu/manual-arm64-*/
~*.md
.cargo-wt-target/
agent-swarm/channel/node_modules/

# vibeos-cli per-machine config override (see .vibeos-cli.local.example.json)
.vibeos-cli.local.json

# WS5 cmake-off orchestrator output (tools/cargo_orchestrate.py)
cmake-off-out/
qemu/snapshots/

# Host-wide build capacity. Seeded from the tracked build-policy.example.json on first
# `vibeos-cli` run, then owned by `vibeos-cli host-policy --apply`. Machine-specific, and
# it lives in the MAIN worktree because it is ONE number for every lane on this host.
/build-policy.json
# Its flock sidecar + atomic-replace temporaries (POLICY_DIR == the main worktree).
/build-policy.lock
/build-policy.paused
/build-policy.*.tmp
